{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345330",
      "title": "Destructuring",
      "sourceHash": "f10e1755514e487f765c6777f29a5e1a37ed804bfd6e0c9784bd995b64c8897a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "Now related to arrays and objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 7.86,
          "en": "there are two crucial,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.86,
          "end": 11.292,
          "en": "relatively new and modern JavaScript features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.292,
          "end": 14.82,
          "en": "you should know because you will also see them quite a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 16.17,
          "en": "throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.17,
          "end": 17.37,
          "en": "And the first feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.37,
          "end": 21.033,
          "en": "is about destructuring arrays and objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 24.21,
          "en": "For that, let's take a look at this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.21,
          "end": 26.76,
          "en": "An array that contains some userNameData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 28.89,
          "en": "The first name and the last name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.89,
          "end": 31.02,
          "en": "Of course, it could be stored in an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.02,
          "end": 32.97,
          "en": "but here it's an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.97,
          "end": 34.47,
          "en": "Now, let's say, in our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.47,
          "end": 37.323,
          "en": "we wanna work with both the first and the last name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.58,
          "end": 40.326,
          "en": "Now what we could do to make it a bit easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.326,
          "end": 42.63,
          "en": "is we could create a new constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.63,
          "end": 45.041,
          "en": "or a variable called firstName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.041,
          "end": 48.6,
          "en": "where we extract the first element of this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 51.273,
          "en": "which is the first name, by using index zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.41,
          "end": 54.48,
          "en": "And then we could add a lastName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.48,
          "end": 56.88,
          "en": "where we also use userNameData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.88,
          "end": 60.9,
          "en": "and use index one to extract the lastName.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.9,
          "end": 61.89,
          "en": "This could be done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.89,
          "end": 64.281,
          "en": "And from now on, we could use firstName and lastName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 64.281,
          "end": 66.955,
          "en": "which is a bit more meaningful than always working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.955,
          "end": 70.563,
          "en": "with userNameData zero and userNameData one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 71.61,
          "end": 74.31,
          "en": "But this code can be shortened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.31,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "Instead of using this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "we could create these two constants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 83.132,
          "en": "or variables in one single step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.132,
          "end": 84.95400000000001,
          "en": "by adding square brackets here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.95400000000001,
          "end": 87.663,
          "en": "on the left side of this equal sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.53,
          "end": 92.28,
          "en": "On the right side, they will create a new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 93.53999999999999,
          "en": "On the left side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 93.53999999999999,
          "end": 95.82,
          "en": "they will destructure that array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.82,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "which simply means that this syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 102.78,
          "en": "can be used to pull values out of this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 102.78,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "And now you can define new constants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 108.66,
          "en": "or variables with any name of your choice here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.66,
          "end": 111.06,
          "en": "And the first constant or variable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.06,
          "end": 113.55,
          "en": "will be mapped to the first array element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.55,
          "end": 117.243,
          "en": "the second one to the second element, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.14,
          "end": 121.86,
          "en": "And this is a super useful syntax since this, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 121.86,
          "end": 125.31,
          "en": "is way shorter to write than what we had before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 130.31,
          "en": "And from now on, I can also console.log firstName",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.52,
          "end": 133.2,
          "en": "and console.log lastName,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 135.36,
          "en": "and use these constants like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.36,
          "end": 139.02,
          "en": "even though the original data is an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.02,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "But due to restructuring,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 142.95,
          "en": "we can pull out these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 142.95,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "and store them in separate constants or variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 149.88,
          "en": "So if I reload this page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 149.88,
          "end": 153.24,
          "en": "I see Max and Schwarzmuller here in the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.24,
          "end": 156.51,
          "en": "because of these two constants that are created with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.51,
          "end": 158.313,
          "en": "of this destructuring syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.27,
          "end": 163.53,
          "en": "Now, this destructuring syntax also exists for objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.53,
          "end": 165.813,
          "en": "We cannot just use it for arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.95,
          "end": 169.44,
          "en": "For that, let's say we had a user object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.44,
          "end": 171.3,
          "en": "that looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.3,
          "end": 173.97,
          "en": "Now again, we might want to store these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.97,
          "end": 176.79,
          "en": "in separate constants or variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 176.79,
          "end": 178.99,
          "en": "For that, of course, we could create a name constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 178.99,
          "end": 182.28,
          "en": "and store user.name inside of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.28,
          "end": 185.55,
          "en": "and an age constant and store user.age inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.55,
          "end": 190.55,
          "en": "That would work, but again, this can be shortened here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.31,
          "end": 193.906,
          "en": "Instead of writing this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.906,
          "end": 196.32,
          "en": "we can again use destructuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.32,
          "end": 199.02,
          "en": "In this case, since we're dealing with an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 199.02,
          "end": 203.94,
          "en": "by writing curly braces on the left side of the equal sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203.94,
          "end": 207.87,
          "en": "On the right side, they will be used to create an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.87,
          "end": 211.41,
          "en": "On the left side, they are used for destructuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.41,
          "end": 213.32999999999998,
          "en": "Just as we used square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213.32999999999998,
          "end": 217.07999999999998,
          "en": "on the left side for destructuring an array before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.07999999999998,
          "end": 220.683,
          "en": "now we're using curly braces to destructure an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 224.91,
          "en": "And then here we can pull out name and age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.91,
          "end": 228.27,
          "en": "Though, these names here are now not up to us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.27,
          "end": 230.164,
          "en": "Instead, we have to use the field names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.164,
          "end": 232.44299999999998,
          "en": "that are defined in the object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 233.55,
          "end": 235.23,
          "en": "For array structuring,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.23,
          "end": 238.07999999999998,
          "en": "these names were up to you because the elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.07999999999998,
          "end": 240.123,
          "en": "were pulled out by position.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 240.96,
          "end": 241.86,
          "en": "For the object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 241.86,
          "end": 245.76,
          "en": "they are pulled out by name, so by property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 245.76,
          "end": 248.71,
          "en": "And therefore you have to use the same property names here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 251.949,
          "en": "Though, you could assign an alias",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 251.949,
          "end": 253.89,
          "en": "by using a colon here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.89,
          "end": 255.9,
          "en": "and then defining your alias name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 255.9,
          "end": 257.553,
          "en": "on the right side of that colon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 258.84,
          "end": 259.971,
          "en": "When creating an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 259.971,
          "end": 261.81,
          "en": "so when using the curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 261.81,
          "end": 263.64,
          "en": "on the right side of the equal sign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 263.64,
          "end": 267.54,
          "en": "the colon is used to separate the key of a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 267.54,
          "end": 269.19,
          "en": "the property name, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 269.19,
          "end": 272.103,
          "en": "from the value that's stored under that property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 273.36,
          "end": 274.505,
          "en": "When using curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 274.505,
          "end": 277.17,
          "en": "on the left side of this equal sign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 277.17,
          "end": 279.15,
          "en": "so when using them for destructuring,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 279.15,
          "end": 280.74,
          "en": "the colon is instead used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 280.74,
          "end": 283.867,
          "en": "for separating the property that's pulled out of this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 283.867,
          "end": 286.863,
          "en": "from the alias name that should be assigned to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 288.96,
          "end": 292.65999999999997,
          "en": "And with that here, we could output userName and age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 295.08,
          "end": 298.563,
          "en": "and we would be using these destructured values for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 299.97,
          "end": 302.43,
          "en": "So therefore, again, if we reload this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 302.43,
          "end": 304.413,
          "en": "we would see these values here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 305.34,
          "end": 307.44,
          "en": "And this destructuring syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 307.44,
          "end": 309.622,
          "en": "really is a crucial JavaScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 309.622,
          "end": 312.03,
          "en": "which we'll use a lot throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 312.03,
          "end": 314.193,
          "en": "And therefore now, you know about it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}